x}=\\infty .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078404 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e806aac-62fc-5c53-a15e-a2ce175dad25" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Open Intervals of Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225115ed-fe14-54a2-9ff7-14b01a6ca201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398850} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c706c6-a7cb-5cbf-a31c-59d0e18e0111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398851} {:answer/id #uuid "0db6826b-749e-538b-898e-9f8e45963932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398852} {:answer/id #uuid "b3965102-b7bf-58c1-9626-978cbd7ed7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398853} {:answer/id #uuid "b32f9c1b-732e-5499-a950-ae4e40e8d8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c706c6-a7cb-5cbf-a31c-59d0e18e0111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398851} :answer-field/id #uuid "134c28b1-b3ff-5d06-b647-ccf5e9b6bae2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b5e7d86-6590-5293-af9e-465db1c9211b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48234" :question/problem "![](images/43/43786cb577705d6ae13d44e75203fef441905e9ccfc3713726f07d36c147c7b3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $y=f(x)$ above continuous? You may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram." :question/worked-solution "To determine the intervals of continuity of a function, we take the domain of the function and exclude any points of discontinuity. \n\nThe function is defined on the interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ The function is discontinuous at $x=-3$ and at $x=3,$ so we need to exclude these points..\n\nTherefore, the function is continuous on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-3),$ $(-3,3),$ and $(-3,\\infty ).$  It is also continuous on any subinterval of these intervals.\n\nAmong the answer choices, the correct one is the following: \n\n$\\,$ $(-\\infty ,-3)$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(-4,-2)$ and $(-\\infty ,1)$ contain the excluded point $-3,$  so the function is not continuous on these intervals.\n\n- $(-2,4)$ and $(2,\\infty )$ contain the excluded point $3,$ so the function is not continuous on these intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078486 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbfddefc-d68b-5b1e-9ec5-fd18be204d92" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Semi-Open Intervals of Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a78c267-c941-5eaa-96d6-33cfa7f0d391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/895c64a995d7f07a161a43945c369395b5cb365c5e7ec0f664df130c49795af8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392624} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff21433-7f43-5f35-8e89-1765d909603a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c24d4207dc777027919d211e4b2262d7340caf25a4166fa004e6e8129da5614.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392625} {:answer/id #uuid "c2952ac4-b61d-5673-a0b6-f777246f57dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c5fedec0f96ef81c33146504cdabc8f0400ba79f77591167a285d119d238fd2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392626} {:answer/id #uuid "e15388cc-ed99-5129-8d21-2895051e2d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7f2b4da10350a6ba230e0ec1b0b26822b133ee4a9c1228a61565ed559efcdd64.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392627} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb4212f-8084-572e-b47a-2ad475a715c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/38/387ed50e8983c83f96ea03bdd7a47d13d33a0c6e0728b52512fef8296351f73e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ff21433-7f43-5f35-8e89-1765d909603a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c24d4207dc777027919d211e4b2262d7340caf25a4166fa004e6e8129da5614.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392625} :answer-field/id #uuid "454e920f-edd9-5ffd-abac-384d24521b07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0790ffcc-e651-53c9-a00a-a9cbd12d21cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-48279" :question/problem "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $(1,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](images/3c/3c24d4207dc777027919d211e4b2262d7340caf25a4166fa004e6e8129da5614.png)\n\nIndeed, we have that $f(x)$ is continuous on the interval $(1,3].$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x)$, $h(x)$,  and $q(x)$ are not right-continuous at $x=3.$\n\n- $p(x)$ is not continuous at  $x=2$, and so is not continuous on $(1,3].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078405 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36524faf-ac61-5756-89e3-c83a947ac61b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Closed Intervals of Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "918d5704-c936-55d5-8203-eac0ffb33b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/72d7fd3effd14aa4449bae360aabd3577846653b5ec364933356e5ba40499cae.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076719} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0d0ca5-e6b9-5a9b-9739-4d0d30653d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b5/b58a88020b68d05c001a188faf7f3c4b1f1b57f8f9a9854d86ec2dc44b6bc347.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076720} {:answer/id #uuid "efa4479b-f8c0-5b64-9dd7-acfb425f9f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/978bb8f022b5a8ff96a47c79c5db11f455511addfaea55cb27f92ccc1c133072.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076721} {:answer/id #uuid "004d454c-d47a-5a5b-a963-7444ffec7a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3dfb0f9b6290f54d1261f0487c738056b7e1cde829ce3df0fb23af262e9e320b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076722} {:answer/id #uuid "561a3430-7984-5ce3-8fad-90a652ccf2ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e57af2e43bd292195f617f60ffed8055891531a2ca5d0249706497d7932d6639.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076723}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e3688b07-cbb6-5b89-9be0-3e7661ec0fe0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f0baec8-e82b-5f18-bfe9-6bb24454a26d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3dfb0f9b6290f54d1261f0487c738056b7e1cde829ce3df0fb23af262e9e320b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392630} {:answer/id #uuid "c1852681-1420-5284-940b-d1399c8a616a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/72d7fd3effd14aa4449bae360aabd3577846653b5ec364933356e5ba40499cae.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392631} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e0a975-3edc-51c3-a886-10ff5f3cfdff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b5/b58a88020b68d05c001a188faf7f3c4b1f1b57f8f9a9854d86ec2dc44b6bc347.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392632} {:answer/id #uuid "58e8cc04-c123-5e69-bb13-8156198731dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e57af2e43bd292195f617f60ffed8055891531a2ca5d0249706497d7932d6639.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392633} {:answer/id #uuid "05aeba16-6981-571b-8fd2-c8fb8c802213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/978bb8f022b5a8ff96a47c79c5db11f455511addfaea55cb27f92ccc1c133072.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58e8cc04-c123-5e69-bb13-8156198731dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e57af2e43bd292195f617f60ffed8055891531a2ca5d0249706497d7932d6639.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392633} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b9e37d1-a2f5-593f-a51a-6ff6525396de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9688522-541f-5cbf-8ad0-7cde48d13425" :question/math-academy-id "q-48293" :question/problem "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $[-1,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is the following. \n\n![](images/e5/e57af2e43bd292195f617f60ffed8055891531a2ca5d0249706497d7932d6639.png)\n\n      \n\nIndeed, this function is continuous on the open intervals $(-\\infty ,2)$ and $(2,\\infty ).$\n\nAdditionally, the function is left-continuous at $x=2.$ Hence, it is continuous on the interval $(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nSo, we can say that the function is continuous on the intervals $(-\\infty ,2]$ and  $(2,\\infty ).$ It is also continuous on any subinterval of these intervals.\n\nTherefore, this function is continuous on $[-1,2],$ because $[-1,2]$ is contained inside the interval $(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $g(x)$ and $p(x)$ are not left-continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- $h(x)$ is not defined at $x=-1,$ and so it is not continuous on the interval $[-1,2].$\n\n- $q(x)$ is not defined at $x=1,$ and so it is not continuous on the interval $[-1,2].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078486 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbfddefc-d68b-5b1e-9ec5-fd18be204d92" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Semi-Open Intervals of Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ef9b73-f52e-5b9c-9db2-9010a5191176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/7225a16c8dfa80bc750607b30c6deb30bb82807365c0c975c6b5ae3e33e11c6f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392637} {:answer/id #uuid "d19ed205-b0ad-5bbb-bcec-dfa49650fec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da6eb0e1cc28a0bef252e0d66bb232006f6a6e54142b27bb04401ca97025af30.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392638} {:answer/id #uuid "f034c628-7593-57d9-af24-2336a12e680e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6c04be0224db916731c3f7b4e2093887ffd36a258b19c4112766125ff435704c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392639} {:answer/id #uuid "899a69d0-95f3-5220-8187-28e906306a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/49356dbd9984d40899b321698d641f200d1d28d498323aa88fdfdfac53ed7910.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392640} {:answer/id #uuid "c336072e-08e4-5982-8f58-51b86e8995ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1326b043af92c5945a5fa679f7daa57eb269ae13edb6d3f9296b3a522678039c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ef9b73-f52e-5b9c-9db2-9010a5191176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/7225a16c8dfa80bc750607b30c6deb30bb82807365c0c975c6b5ae3e33e11c6f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392637} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4d2a845-2450-5e73-b0b2-bcfee6b03964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c74056bd-b0fc-5dc2-914f-2bbc6b987726" :question/math-academy-id "q-48348" :question/problem "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $(-\\infty ,-1]?$  You may assume that all points of discontinuity for each function are shown." :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](images/72/7225a16c8dfa80bc750607b30c6deb30bb82807365c0c975c6b5ae3e33e11c6f.png)\n\nWe see that $h(x)$ is continuous on the interval $(-\\infty ,0],$ and since $(-\\infty ,-1]$ lies completely inside $(-\\infty ,0],$ it is also continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1].$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are not continuous at $x=-2$, and so are not continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1].$\n\n- $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are not continuous at $x=-3$, and so are not continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1].$"}]}
